    {
      "type": "intro",
      "heading": "Family in Punjabi life",
      "body": "Family is central in Punjabi culture, and family words come up constantly in conversation — \"this is my mother\", \"I have three brothers\", \"my grandmother lives with us\".\n\nOne important thing to know early: Punjabi kinship words are more specific than English. Your father's brother and your mother's brother have different names. This lesson covers the core words; the detailed uncle/aunt map comes later."
    },
